## Key Concepts

- Real-time streaming: Kinesis Data Streams and Lambda
- AI processing: Amazon Comprehend, SageMaker endpoint
- Data storage and protection: S3 versioning, SSE-KMS
- State and queries: DynamoDB index
- Reliability and cost: DLQ, backpressure, shard sizing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lambda handler sketch
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const comprehend = new AWS.Comprehend();
const sagemaker = new AWS.SageMakerRuntime();

exports.handler = async (event) => {
  for (const rec of event.Records) {
    const msg = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(rec.kinesis.data, 'base64').toString());
    const { Text } = msg;
    const sit = await comprehend.detectSentiment({ Text, LanguageCode: 'en' }).promise();
    const kp = await comprehend.detectKeyPhrases({ Text, LanguageCode: 'en' }).promise();
    const resp = await sagemaker.invokeEndpoint({ EndpointName: 'ComplianceClassifier', Body: JSON.stringify({ text: Text }), ContentType: 'application/json' }).promise();
    // Persist and upsert logic omitted for brevity
  }
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle model drift and monitoring for the SageMaker classifier?
- How would you enforce data residency and access controls across regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design an end-to-end, privacy-aware, event-driven pipeline on AWS using basic services.

## Key Concepts
- S3 event triggers and Lambda integration
- Amazon Comprehend for sentiment, entities, and PII
- Redaction patterns and data privacy controls
- Separate storage for redacted transcripts and analytics
- DynamoDB upsert for fast lookups
- IAM, encryption (SSE-KMS), access logs, retries

## Code Example
```javascript
import { ComprehendClient, DetectSentimentCommand, DetectEntitiesCommand, DetectPiiEntitiesCommand } from '@aws-sdk/client-comprehend';

const client = new ComprehendClient({ region: 'us-east-1' });

async function analyze(text) {
  const sentiment = await client.send(new DetectSentimentCommand({ Text: text, LanguageCode: 'EN' }));
  const entities = await client.send(new DetectEntitiesCommand({ Text: text, LanguageCode: 'EN' }));
  const pii = await client.send(new DetectPiiEntitiesCommand({ Text: text, LanguageCode: 'EN' }));
  return { sentiment: sentiment.Sentiment, entities: entities.Entities, pii: pii.Entities };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement idempotency and retries in the Lambda to avoid duplicates?
- How would you test privacy controls and monitor costs at this scale?

## Why This Question Is Asked
Tests ability to design a privacy-aware, multi-stage pipeline with governance and cross-account considerations.

## Key Concepts
- Event-driven architecture; S3 event filtering; Transcribe with diarization; Comprehend PII redaction; SageMaker multi-task inference; DynamoDB composite keys; KMS encryption; Glue lineage; DLQ design; cross-account IAM trust policies.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Orchestrator triggered on S3 PUT event
async function handle(event) {
  const { bucket, key } = event.Records[0].s3;
  const callId = extractCallId(key);
  const transcribeJob = await startTranscribe(bucket, key, callId);
  await pollUntilComplete(transcribeJob.JobId, onTranscribeComplete);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate privacy guarantees end-to-end and simulate PII leakage scenarios?
- How would you detect and mitigate model drift across languages in production?
- What retry and timeout strategies would you implement for each service call?

